:0,"endColumn":55,"endLine":82,"line":71},"type":102,"typeText":"{α : Type u_1} →\n  {motive : Filter.{u_1} α → Sort u} →\n    ((sets : Set.{u_1} (Set.{u_1} α)) →\n        (univ_sets : Membership.mem.{u_1, u_1} sets Set.univ.{u_1}) →\n          (sets_of_superset :\n              ∀ {x y : Set.{u_1} α},\n                Membership.mem.{u_1, u_1} sets x → HasSubset.Subset.{u_1} x y → Membership.mem.{u_1, u_1} sets y) →\n            (inter_sets :\n                ∀ {x y : Set.{u_1} α},\n                  Membership.mem.{u_1, u_1} sets x →\n                    Membership.mem.{u_1, u_1} sets y → Membership.mem.{u_1, u_1} sets (Inter.inter.{u_1} x y)) →\n              motive (Filter.mk.{u_1} sets univ_sets sets_of_superset inter_sets)) →\n      (t : Filter.{u_1} α) → motive t","unsafe":false,"value":null,"source":{"code":"/-- A filter `F` on a type `α` is a collection of sets of `α` which contains the whole `α`,\nis upwards-closed, and is stable under intersection. We do not forbid this collection to be\nall sets of `α`. -/\nstructure Filter (α : Type*) where\n  /-- The set of sets that belong to the filter. -/\n  sets : Set (Set α)\n  /-- The set `Set.univ` belongs to any filter. -/\n  univ_sets : Set.univ ∈ sets\n  /-- If a set belongs to a filter, then its superset belongs to the filter as well. -/\n  sets_of_superset {x y} : x ∈ sets → x ⊆ y → y ∈ sets\n  /-- If two sets belong to a filter, then their intersection belongs to the filter as well. -/\n  inter_sets {x y} : x ∈ sets → y ∈ sets → x ∩ y ∈ sets","start":71,"end":82},"axioms":[]}